    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for basil beef with coconut rice. The Thai spot down the street charges $15 for a smaller portion, and they keep the leftovers.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "The 93/7 ground beef is the big line at 3.5 pounds. Leaner beef costs more per pound but you are not paying to drain fat down the sink, which matters when the sauce needs to cling.",
                       "Canned coconut milk is one of the most price-volatile items in the store. Stock up when it goes on sale, it keeps for ages in the pantry.",
                       "Skip the pre-shredded carrots. Whole carrots cost less for what this recipe needs and shred in under two minutes with a box grater."
